      "writtenOn": "2022-11-14T06:00:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see. I hope we can improve the naming of `.[use|is]Vndk()` in the future, as I think the definition is all pretty weird:\n\nuseVndk() returns true for vendor and product variant libraries.\nisVndk() return true for libraries that _have a variant that is vndk_. If a library have both platform and vendor-vndk variant, both variants return true!\n\nthat said reviewing (and fixing) all the existing occurrences of `isVndk()` is large work with lots of friction, so I\u0027m okay with open coding `ctx.useVndk() \u0026\u0026 ctx.isVndk()` here like this.\n\nA low hanging fruit might be to rename `isVndk()` to `hasVndkVariant()`\nadd something another helper method `isVndkVariant()` which returns `ctx.useVndk() \u0026\u0026 ctx.hasVndkVariant()`?",
      "parentUuid": "ade8949a_449e0e5a",
      "revId": "a90bd389c51a5e99d5d898ed82ab231a89064293",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
